"notes": "Modified cash basis school district; read pages 1-21 of 21 (trimmed). All lines governmental (Total Governmental Funds column, p4-5); School Nutrition is reported within Other Governmental Funds (no separate proprietary statement), so no business-type section. Transfers in/out 162,544 each (total column); the 180,000 interfund loan between General and Special Building nets to zero in the total column and is not recorded at top level. Roll-forward: 2,388,767 + 7,149,273 - 6,850,891 + 162,544 - 162,544 = 2,687,149. Balance sheet = Statement of Activities and Net Position (p3) total governmental activities column (cash basis, no liabilities). Detail: General Fund combining schedule (p7) not recorded; General Fund budget-and-actual schedule (p8-10) used instead (General Fund alone; Depreciation and Employee Benefit funds recorded from their own schedules p12-13). Hidden transfer fixed (attempt 2): General Fund 2500 Central services 358,664 includes 2,325 paid to the Employee Benefit Fund (Employee Benefit 'Transfer - General Fund (as expensed from the General Fund)' 2,325, p13; General Fund combining schedule Reclassifications (2,325), p7), so the line is recorded as 356,339 expenditure plus -2,325 other financing; GF detail total 5,653,232 (includes other financing) is unchanged in sum. Statement Central services 359,252 = 358,664 - 2,325 + Employee Benefit benefits paid 2,913. Label conflict: 24,030 is 'Loan proceeds' on the government-wide statement (p2) but 'Insurance adjustments' on the fund statement (p4) and GF schedule 5301 (p10); the fund-level label is kept (reimbursements/refunds, not debt proceeds) and flagged for review. General Fund schedule lines with a budget but no 2025 actual (ESU receipts, 3990 other state receipts, Depreciation Fund transfer/general supplies/capital outlay, QCPU purchased services) were skipped; Cooperative Fund has no 2025 activity. Read pages 1-21 of 21."
